---
import Article from '../../layouts/Article.astro'
import AssertionCard from '../../components/AssertionCard.astro'
import ChartFigure from '../../components/ChartFigure.astro'
import Gloss from '../../components/Gloss.astro'
import { assertion } from '../../lib/feeds'
import { bar, line } from '../../lib/chart-spec'

const all = assertion('a-hundred-and-twelve-questions')
const renews = assertion('the-county-renews-and-does-not-add')
const notOne = assertion('the-renewal-that-failed-was-not-one')
const replacement = assertion('a-replacement-passes-like-a-renewal')
const bonds = assertion('new-borrowing-is-the-hardest-ask')
const beaverdam = assertion('beaverdam-refused-three-times')
const notMoney = assertion('everything-not-about-money-passed')
const busiest = assertion('the-busiest-ballot-was-an-odd-year')
const surrender = assertion('the-village-surrendered-its-corporate-power')
const refused = assertion('fort-shawnee-refused-to-pay-then-dissolved')
const witnesses = assertion('two-instruments-put-the-end-in-the-same-year')
const survey = assertion('the-survey-misses-what-a-government-gives-up')
const liquor = assertion('thirty-liquor-questions-precinct-by-precinct')
const restaurants = assertion('an-olive-garden-and-a-red-lobster')
const twoVotes = assertion('carried-by-two-votes')
const twoAnswers = assertion('one-precinct-two-answers')
const forms = assertion('no-report-says-what-the-forms-ask')
const elsewhere = assertion('thirteen-questions-filed-elsewhere')
const attribution = assertion('a-return-under-a-county-is-not-its-vote')
const elida = assertion('the-elida-return-cannot-be-right')

const levySpec = bar(
  ['renewal', 'replacement', 'additional'],
  [97.8, 100.0, 35.3],
  { yTitle: 'Questions passed, per cent', tickSuffix: '%', labelValues: true },
)

const typeSpec = bar(
  ['tax levy', 'electric aggregation', 'school income tax', 'bond issue', 'municipal income tax'],
  [88.7, 87.5, 58.3, 37.5, 20.0],
  { yTitle: 'Questions passed, per cent', tickSuffix: '%', labelValues: true },
)

const days = ['2003-05', '2004-03', '2004-08', '2004-11', '2005-05', '2005-08', '2005-11', '2006-11', '2007-05', '2007-08', '2007-11', '2009-05', '2010-11', '2011-05', '2011-11', '2012-11']
const asked = [5, 9, 1, 2, 4, 1, 4, 16, 8, 1, 10, 8, 7, 5, 19, 12]
const passed = [5, 6, 0, 2, 4, 0, 3, 12, 5, 0, 8, 7, 6, 4, 18, 8]

const daySpec = line(
  days,
  [
    { name: 'questions put', y: asked },
    { name: 'questions passed', y: passed },
  ],
  { yTitle: 'Ballot questions', labelLast: true, zeroBased: true },
)
---

<Article slug="the-back-of-the-ballot">
  <p>
    Under the candidates on an Ohio ballot there is a second election nobody campaigns across the
    state about. It renews a fire levy, borrows for a school roof, raises an income tax by four
    tenths of a point, decides whether a filling station may sell beer, and occasionally asks a
    village whether it would like to go on being one. The Secretary of State compiled the returns
    election by election, category by category, and then stopped serving them; ninety of the reports
    survive in the Internet Archive, and they cover sixteen election days in this county.
  </p>
  <AssertionCard assertion={all} open />

  <h2>Renew, replace, but do not add</h2>
  <AssertionCard assertion={renews} />
  <ChartFigure
    id="levies"
    title="Sixty-two points between the same money and more of it"
    caption="Share of Allen County's tax and bond questions that passed, by the word the ballot uses for what it is asking. Forty-five renewals, thirteen replacements and seventeen additional levies, 2003 to 2012."
    columns={['What it asks', 'Put', 'Passed', 'Mean yes share']}
    rows={[
      ['renewal', '45', '44', '64.9%'],
      ['replacement', '13', '13', '64.3%'],
      ['additional', '17', '6', '47.0%'],
      ['not stated in those words', '5', '3', '49.4%'],
    ]}
    height={280}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="levies" set:html={JSON.stringify(levySpec)} is:inline />
  <AssertionCard assertion={notOne} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={replacement} />
  <Gloss>
    A renewal re-levies the same millage against the valuation the tax reduction factors froze it
    at, so it collects about what it collected. A replacement re-levies the same millage against
    current valuation, so it collects more. The ballot prints both words and this electorate treated
    them the same — thirteen replacements, thirteen passed, at a mean yes share within six tenths of
    a point of the renewals'. The word that moved votes was <em>additional</em>, and what it names
    is not a larger tax than a replacement so much as a more legible one.
  </Gloss>
  <AssertionCard assertion={bonds} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={beaverdam} />
  <ChartFigure
    id="types"
    title="What the county says yes to"
    caption="Share passed by kind of question, Allen County, 2003 to 2012. Charter amendments, a zoning referendum and two ordinances by petition are not drawn: all six of them passed."
    columns={['Question', 'Put', 'Passed']}
    rows={[
      ['tax levy', '71', '63'],
      ['school income tax', '12', '7'],
      ['bond issue', '8', '3'],
      ['electric aggregation', '8', '7'],
      ['municipal income tax', '5', '1'],
      ['charter amendment', '3', '3'],
      ['ordinance or referendum', '2', '2'],
      ['zoning referendum', '1', '1'],
      ['disincorporation', '1', '1'],
      ['combined bond and levy', '1', '0'],
    ]}
    height={300}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="types" set:html={JSON.stringify(typeSpec)} is:inline />
  <AssertionCard assertion={notMoney} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={busiest} />
  <ChartFigure
    id="elections"
    title="Sixteen ballots"
    caption="Local questions put and passed at each election in the record. The two August specials carried one question each and both failed; the nineteen of November 2011 are the most this county has decided at once."
    columns={['Election', 'Put', 'Passed']}
    rows={days.map((d, i) => [d, asked[i], passed[i]])}
    height={300}
  />
  <script type="application/json" data-chart-spec="elections" set:html={JSON.stringify(daySpec)} is:inline />

  <h2>A village stops</h2>
  <AssertionCard assertion={refused} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={surrender} open />
  <Gloss>
    This one had been an open question here since the first week of the corpus. The Census Bureau
    listed Fort Shawnee as a village in 2010 and as a census designated place in 2020, and a village
    is a government while a CDP is a shape on a map. Four records narrowed it: a roster of
    governments that carried the village in 2012 and not in 2017, a gazetteer that redrew it between
    the 2012 and 2013 vintages, a county Auditor's tax set that levied village millage in tax year
    2012 and none in 2013, and a boundary file that turned out to be the gazetteer again rather than
    a fourth witness. Between them they said the corporation ended in some twelve months and could
    not say how. It ended on a Tuesday in November, on a petition, by 200 votes.
  </Gloss>
  <AssertionCard assertion={witnesses} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={survey} />

  <h2>Liquor, by the precinct</h2>
  <AssertionCard assertion={liquor} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={restaurants} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={twoVotes} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={twoAnswers} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={forms} />

  <h2>What the file will not answer</h2>
  <AssertionCard assertion={attribution} />
  <AssertionCard assertion={elsewhere} />
  <Gloss>
    The convention is one line at the head of every page: an asterisk denotes the most populous
    county. A school district that crosses a county line is listed once, under whichever county
    holds most of it, with the whole district's vote. So a question filed under this county's
    heading in November 2012 carries 48,543 votes, and the county cast 48,708 ballots that day on
    every office and question together — the number belongs to six counties. It runs the other way
    too: thirteen questions Allen County's voters answered are printed under Putnam or Auglaize,
    because Allen is the smaller partner there. A yes share survives the convention. A vote count
    does not.
  </Gloss>
  <AssertionCard assertion={elida} />
</Article>
